				}
			},
			{
				"box": {
					"code": "/*\r\n * sr.blur.circular.genjit\r\n *\r\n * Circular disk blur (bokeh-like effect)\r\n * Part of SevenRad Max 8 Effects\r\n *\r\n * Parameters:\r\n *   radius (int 0-30): Disk radius in pixels\r\n *\r\n * Algorithm:\r\n *   - Uniform averaging over circular disk\r\n *   - Tests each point in bounding box: x^2 + y^2 <= r^2\r\n *   - All samples have equal weight (box blur)\r\n *\r\n * Performance:\r\n *   O(r^2) per pixel - may be slow for large radii.\r\n *   Consider using separable blur for large sigma values.\r\n *\r\n * Visual Effect:\r\n *   Creates smooth, circular bokeh-like blur.\r\n *   Different from Gaussian blur (no edge falloff).\r\n *\r\n * Source: src/sevenrad_stills/operations/blur_circular_taichi.py\r\n */\r\n\r\n\r\n// Accumulator for color sum\r\nsum = vec(0, 0, 0, 0);\r\ncount = 0;\r\n\r\n// Iterate over bounding box of the circular disk\r\nfor (y = -radius; y <= radius; y += 1) {\r\n    for (x = -radius; x <= radius; x += 1) {\r\n        // Check if point is inside circular disk\r\n        // Using integer comparison to match reference implementation\r\n        if (x*x + y*y <= radius*radius) {\r\n            // Convert pixel offset to normalized coordinates\r\n            offset = vec(float(x) / dim.x, float(y) / dim.y);\r\n\r\n            // Sample and accumulate\r\n            sum += sample(in1, norm + offset);\r\n            count += 1;\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Average all samples (uniform weighting)\r\nout1 = sum / max(float(count), 1.0);",
					"fontname": "Arial",
					"fontsize": 12.0,
					"id": "obj-3",
					"maxclass": "codebox",
					"numinlets": 1,
					"numoutlets": 1,
